# Environment variables
# ============================================================================
#  You do not need this file to run Griha.
#
#  Clone, `npm install`, `npm run dev`. With no configuration at all the app
#  starts an embedded Postgres (PGlite) in the same process, so the board, the
#  fairness report, the agent console and every export work immediately.
#
#  Copy to `.env.local` only if you want to change something below.
# ============================================================================


# --- Database ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed if you want data to survive a restart or a redeploy. Any hosted
# Postgres works: Neon, Vercel Postgres, Supabase, RDS. Postgres 14+.
#
# Use the pooled (-pooler) host with the Neon serverless driver.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require
#
# POSTGRES_URL is used automatically when DATABASE_URL is unset, because that is
# the variable the Vercel Postgres and Neon marketplace integrations create. If
# you installed one of those, you do not need to set anything by hand.
#
# The app deliberately refuses to start in production without a connection
# string rather than falling back to the embedded database, which would lose
# every household on the next cold start.


# --- Database schema -------------------------------------------------------
# Which Postgres schema to put the tables in. Defaults to `public`.
#
# Set this when you share one database with another application so the tables are
# namespaced instead of colliding. Must be a bare identifier: lowercase letters,
# digits and underscores only, not starting with a digit. Anything else is
# rejected at startup rather than interpolated into SQL.
# DATABASE_SCHEMA=griha


# --- Embedded database escape hatch (development only) ---------------------
# Griha will not silently fall back to an embedded database in production.
#
# Setting this to 1 opts in explicitly, which is useful for running a production
# build on a laptop with no database at all:
#
#   npm run build && ALLOW_EMBEDDED_DB=1 npm start
#
# The database lives in the process and is gone when it exits. `/api/health`
# reports `"durable": false` whenever this is active, so a deployment using it
# can never be mistaken for a durable one. Never set this on a real deployment.
# ALLOW_EMBEDDED_DB=1


# --- Rate limiting ---------------------------------------------------------
# Griha applies a small per-process write throttle to anonymous sessions so a
# single address cannot flood the store. On serverless, instances do not share
# memory, so this only bounds traffic that lands on one warm instance.
#
# For a hard limit, put a hosted rate limiter (Vercel KV / Upstash, Cloudflare
# WAF, or an API gateway) in front of /api/*. No key is needed for Griha itself;
# the limiter is infrastructure you choose to add.
#
# WRITES_PER_MINUTE is not read by Griha — the limit is fixed at 40 and
# documented here so the ceiling is not a surprise.


# --- The public URL --------------------------------------------------------
# There is deliberately no variable for this. Set `site.url` in
# src/config/site.ts instead, because that value also produces the canonical
# URLs, the OpenGraph tags, the sitemap, the web manifest and the QR code on the
# install page. Keeping it next to the rest of the product identity means one
# file to edit, and the deploy step rewrites it from the real Vercel alias.